  "sources": {
    "INSTRUCTIONS.md": {
      "state": "current",
      "versions": [
        {
          "commit": "57f541c",
          "date": "2026-10-24",
          "hash": "f762e7650270073d828bdee60efe9c2cbaf4479a375598dc2b0ecbec9d762f3b",
          "release": "",
          "state": "consumed",
          "via": "plan",
          "ticket": null,
          "requirements": [
            {
              "name": "python-service-stack",
              "text": "Implement in Python 3.11 or newer with FastAPI, served by uvicorn, over SQLite.",
              "stories": [
                "architecture",
                "serve_api"
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "executable",
              "text": "The product is an executable named `fxrates` at the application root.",
              "stories": [
                "architecture",
                "initialize_store",
                "load_history",
                "fetch_history",
                "serve_api"
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "initialize-rates-table",
              "text": "`fxrates init` | Drops the `rates` table if present and creates it empty. | Nothing.",
              "stories": [
                "database",
                "initialize_store"
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "load-ecb-history",
              "text": "`fxrates load <csv>` | Loads an ECB history file (rules below). | `dates,rates`, then the number of dates and of rates stored from the file.",
              "stories": [
                "database",
                "load_history"
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "fetch-ecb-history",
              "text": "`fxrates fetch` | Downloads `https://www.ecb.europa.eu/stats/eurofxref/eurofxref-hist.zip`, extracts `eurofxref-hist.csv`, and loads it as `load` does. | As `load`.",
              "stories": [
                "fetch_history",
                "load_history"
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "serve-http-api",
              "text": "`fxrates serve [--port <n>]` | Serves the HTTP API on `127.0.0.1:<n>` with uvicorn until stopped. Default port `8000`. | Nothing required.",
              "stories": [
                "serve_api",
                "architecture"
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "validate-ecb-csv-format",
              "text": "1. The file is CSV. The header's first field is `Date`, and every other field is a three-letter uppercase currency code. The ECB writes a trailing comma on every line, and the resulting empty last field is ignored.\n2. Each row is a date (`YYYY-MM-DD`, a real calendar date, not repeated within the file) followed by one value per currency. The value `N/A` means no rate, and nothing is stored for it. Any other value must match `[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?` and be nonzero.",
              "stories": [
                "load_history"
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "atomic-load-rejects-invalid-file",
              "text": "3. **A rejected file changes nothing.** The whole file is checked before the first write. A row with the wrong field count, an invalid or repeated date, or an invalid value rejects the file.",
              "stories": [
                "load_history",
                "database"
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "replace-existing-rates",
              "text": "4. A rate for a (`date`, `currency`) that is already stored replaces it, so loading the same file twice leaves the database unchanged.",
              "stories": [
                "load_history",
                "database"
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "report-load-counts",
              "text": "5. The reported `dates` counts the dates with at least one stored rate, and `rates` counts the rates stored.",
              "stories": [
                "load_history"
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "cli-failure-diagnostics-and-codes",
              "text": "A failing command writes nothing to standard output and one diagnostic line to standard error.",
              "stories": [
                "cli_errors",
                "load_history",
                "fetch_history"
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "cli-exit-codes",
              "text": "**Exit codes.** `0` success. `1` operational failure: the file cannot be read, or a `fetch` download fails. `2` usage error: unknown command, wrong argument count, `--port` not an integer. `3` rejected file.",
              "stories": [
                "cli_errors",
                "load_history",
                "fetch_history",
                "serve_api"
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "health-endpoint",
              "text": "`GET /health` | `{\"status\": \"ok\"}`",
              "stories": [
                "api_health_stats"
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "stats-endpoint",
              "text": "`GET /stats` | `{\"dates\": <n>, \"rates\": <n>, \"first\": <date>, \"last\": <date>}`. `first` and `last` are `null` when the table is empty.",
              "stories": [
                "api_health_stats",
                "database"
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "currencies-endpoint",
              "text": "`GET /currencies` | `{\"base\": \"EUR\", \"currencies\": [<code>, ...]}`: every currency with at least one stored rate, ascending.",
              "stories": [
                "api_currencies",
                "database"
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "rates-endpoint",
              "text": "`GET /rates/{date}` | `{\"date\": <effective date>, \"requested\": <date>, \"base\": \"EUR\", \"rates\": {<code>: <rate>, ...}}`: every currency with a rate on the effective date.",
              "stories": [
                "api_rates",
                "database"
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "latest-rates-endpoint",
              "text": "`GET /rates/latest` | As `/rates/{date}` for the latest publication date, with `\"requested\": \"latest\"`.",
              "stories": [
                "api_rates",
                "database"
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "convert-endpoint",
              "text": "`GET /convert?from=<code>&to=<code>&amount=<amount>[&date=<date>]` | `{\"date\": <effective date>, \"from\": <code>, \"to\": <code>, \"amount\": <amount>, \"rate\": <rate>, \"result\": <result>}`. Without `date`, the latest publication date is used.",
              "stories": [
                "api_convert",
                "database"
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "history-endpoint",
              "text": "`GET /history/{code}[?start=<date>][&end=<date>]` | `{\"currency\": <code>, \"base\": \"EUR\", \"count\": <n>, \"min\": <rate>, \"max\": <rate>, \"mean\": <mean>, \"points\": [{\"date\": <date>, \"rate\": <rate>}, ...]}` for the publication dates from `start` through `end` inclusive, ascending. Both bounds are optional. With no points, `count` is `0`, `min`, `max`, and `mean` are `null`, and `points` is `[]`.",
              "stories": [
                "api_history",
                "database"
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "rate-storage-and-decimal-arithmetic",
              "text": "A rate is stored exactly as the ECB publishes it, as text. `0.943` stays `0.943`, never `0.9430` and never a float. Arithmetic on rates uses Python's `decimal` module.",
              "stories": [
                "database",
                "api_convert",
                "api_history"
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "convert-amount-and-rounding",
              "text": "- `/convert` `amount` matches `[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?` and is echoed as given, as a JSON string.\n- `/convert` `rate` is `rate(to) / rate(from)`, computed exactly and rounded half to even to six\n  decimal places, written with exactly six decimals, as a JSON string: `\"161.770000\"`.\n- `/convert` `result` is `amount \u00d7 rate(to) / rate(from)`, computed exactly from the stored rates\n  (not from the rounded `rate`) and rounded half to even to two decimal places, written with\n  exactly two decimals, as a JSON string: `\"82.01\"`.",
              "stories": [
                "api_convert"
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "history-summary-rules",
              "text": "- `/history` `min` and `max` are the stored text of the smallest and largest rate by value.\n  `mean` is the exact mean rounded half to even to six decimal places, written with exactly six\n  decimals, as a JSON string.",
              "stories": [
                "api_history"
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "http-error-statuses",
              "text": "| Status | Condition |\n|---|---|\n| `404` | No publication on or before the requested date; a `/convert` currency other than EUR with no rate on the effective date; a `/history` currency with no stored rate at all (including `EUR`). |\n| `422` | A malformed date in the path or query, a malformed `amount`, or a missing required query parameter. FastAPI's request validation produces this status. |",
              "stories": [
                "api_rates",
                "api_convert",
                "api_history"
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "live-load-visibility",
              "text": "A load that completes while the server is running is visible to the next request.",
              "stories": [
                "load_history",
                "serve_api"
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "test-suite",
              "text": "The completed application provides a POSIX-compatible `bin/test.sh` that runs its own pytest suite from the application root and exits zero only when every test passes. The suite covers each command, each load rule, each endpoint, the effective-date rule, rounding, and each error status, against a real temporary database, with `fetch` stubbed.",
              "stories": [
                "conformance"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
